# OpsHub web — dev env.
#
# Deliberately almost empty, and `VITE_API_URL` is deliberately ABSENT: the SPA calls
# relative /v1 paths and must be same-origin with the API, because authentication rides a
# `__Secure-` session cookie that identity 8 sets on the SPA host and that cannot be set cross-site. Locally the Vite proxy provides
# that (/v1 and /api/auth → :3001); deployed, the Cloudflare Pages Functions do
# (apps/web/functions/v1/[[path]].ts and functions/api/auth/[[path]].ts). Setting VITE_API_URL to the API host would send the
# browser straight there and silently break login while reads kept working.
#
# No Entra values here any more. The SPA runs no OIDC flow — MSAL is gone, and so are the
# tokens it produced. `POST /api/auth/sign-in/social` (identity 8) starts the Authorization-Code + PKCE flow
# SERVER-side, so the tenant id, client id and client secret live only in the API's config
# (see the root .env.example).
